Throwing this out in case it is actually still an issue when I get on later today;

When I was last playing, I spent a while trying to land a vertical takeoff and landing dropship on a celestial body made with a specific mod. It was badly balanced, and I went through a bunch of attempts before it finally survived landing and I got it docked to my base. But for some reason, even when the ship was totally stopped, and when it no longer existed and had been joined to the base, I kept getting the 'cannot save collision course' warning as I tried to exit.

The game was still auto-saving after certain actions, and it saved with the base attached together, but I'm wondering if this is something I'm going to keep having or if anyone else has experienced it. My only other vessels are three satellites in orbit around the celestial body, all functioning well.
